<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendices</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Digital Twin of Oxygenation Dynamics: Synthetic Physiology and Observation</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We constructed a digital twin of pulmonary gas exchange, evolving over discrete minutes
<math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=720" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>720</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=720</annotation></semantics></math>. At the halfway point <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\star}=360" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>360</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\star}=360</annotation></semantics></math>, a regime change (“phase transition”) in lung physiology is triggered.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At each time <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> the recorded parameters are inspired oxygen fraction (FiO<sub id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>),
positive end-expiratory pressure (PEEP), tidal volume (VT, mL), respiratory rate
(RR, breaths/min), a proning indicator, and lung compliance
(CL, mL/cmH<sub id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O). Constants are fixed as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{b}=760\;\text{(mmHg)},\quad P_{H_{2}O}=47\;\text{(mmHg)},\quad R=0.8,\quad V_{\text{CO}_{2}}=200\;\text{(mL/min)},\quad\text{SvO}_{2}=0.70," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>760</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>(mmHg)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>47</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>(mmHg)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mtext>CO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>200</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>(mL/min)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>SvO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.70</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{b}=760\;\text{(mmHg)},\quad P_{H_{2}O}=47\;\text{(mmHg)},\quad R=0.8,\quad V_{\text{CO}_{2}}=200\;\text{(mL/min)},\quad\text{SvO}_{2}=0.70,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">together with a Hill dissociation curve defined by <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P50=26.6\;\text{(mmHg)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>26.6</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>(mmHg)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P50=26.6\;\text{(mmHg)}</annotation></semantics></math> and Hill coefficient <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2.7</annotation></semantics></math>, predicted body weight <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{PBW}=70\;\text{(Kg)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>PBW</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>70</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>(Kg)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{PBW}=70\;\text{(Kg)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and anatomic dead space <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{VD}_{\text{anat}}=2.2\cdot\text{PBW}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>VD</mtext><mtext>anat</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>PBW</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{VD}_{\text{anat}}=2.2\cdot\text{PBW}</annotation></semantics></math> (mL).</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Regime schedule.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A logistic transition variable increases sigmoidally after <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g(t)=\frac{1}{1+\exp\!\bigl(-\tfrac{t-t^{\star}}{\tau_{g}}\bigr)},\quad\tau_{g}\in[12,20]\text{ minutes (case-specific).}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> minutes (case-specific).</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g(t)=\frac{1}{1+\exp\!\bigl(-\tfrac{t-t^{\star}}{\tau_{g}}\bigr)},\quad\tau_{g}\in[12,20]\text{ minutes (case-specific).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This regime modulates several parameters: compliance falls, alveolar dead space and shunt
rise, and the A–a gradient worsens. PEEP and proning try to mitigate these effects.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Alveolar ventilation and PaCO<sub id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Auto-PEEP fraction <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\text{auto}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>auto</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\text{auto}}</annotation></semantics></math> increases with tachypnea and low compliance:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi_{\text{auto}}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(k_{RR}\bigl(RR(t)-14\bigr)+k_{CL}\bigl(35-CL(t)\bigr),0,0.08\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>auto</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>35</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.08</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi_{\text{auto}}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(k_{RR}\bigl(RR(t)-14\bigr)+k_{CL}\bigl(35-CL(t)\bigr),0,0.08\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with typical <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{RR}=0.002" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.002</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{RR}=0.002</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{CL}=0.004" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.004</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{CL}=0.004</annotation></semantics></math> pre-transition, and the clipping operator <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(x,a,b\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(x,a,b\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> restricting a value <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to the interval <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(x,a,b\bigr)=\min(\max(x,a),b)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(x,a,b\bigr)=\min(\max(x,a),b).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then, the effective and alveolar tidal volumes are:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{VT}_{\text{eff}}(t)=\text{VT}(t)\bigl(1-\phi_{\text{auto}}(t)\bigr),\quad\text{VT}_{\text{alv}}(t)=\max\bigl(\text{VT}_{\text{eff}}(t)-\text{VD}_{\text{anat}}-f_{DS}(t)\,\text{VT}_{\text{eff}}(t),\,5\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>VT</mtext><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>VT</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>auto</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>VT</mtext><mtext>alv</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>VT</mtext><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mtext>VD</mtext><mtext>anat</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>VT</mtext><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{VT}_{\text{eff}}(t)=\text{VT}(t)\bigl(1-\phi_{\text{auto}}(t)\bigr),\quad\text{VT}_{\text{alv}}(t)=\max\bigl(\text{VT}_{\text{eff}}(t)-\text{VD}_{\text{anat}}-f_{DS}(t)\,\text{VT}_{\text{eff}}(t),\,5\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where alveolar dead-space fraction depends on regime <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and PEEP</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{DS}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(0.10\bigl(1-g(t)\bigr)+0.25\,g(t)-0.005\,g(t)\,\bigl(\text{PEEP}(t)-5\bigr),0.05,0.35\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0.10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.005</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>PEEP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.35</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{DS}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(0.10\bigl(1-g(t)\bigr)+0.25\,g(t)-0.005\,g(t)\,\bigl(\text{PEEP}(t)-5\bigr),0.05,0.35\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Alveolar ventilation (L/min) and arterial CO<sub id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub> follow:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{A}(t)=\frac{\text{VT}_{\text{alv}}(t)\cdot RR(t)}{1000},\qquad\text{PaCO}_{2}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(\frac{863\,V_{\text{CO}_{2}}}{\max(V_{A}(t),\,0.5)},25,80\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>VT</mtext><mtext>alv</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>1000</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>PaCO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>863</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mtext>CO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>80</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{A}(t)=\frac{\text{VT}_{\text{alv}}(t)\cdot RR(t)}{1000},\qquad\text{PaCO}_{2}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(\frac{863\,V_{\text{CO}_{2}}}{\max(V_{A}(t),\,0.5)},25,80\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Alveolar O<sub id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub> and A–a gradient.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Alveolar oxygen tension derives from the alveolar gas equation:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{A}O_{2}(t)=\text{FiO}_{2}(t)\bigl(P_{b}-P_{H_{2}O}\bigr)-\frac{\text{PaCO}_{2}(t)}{R}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>FiO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>PaCO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{A}O_{2}(t)=\text{FiO}_{2}(t)\bigl(P_{b}-P_{H_{2}O}\bigr)-\frac{\text{PaCO}_{2}(t)}{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A–a gradient increases with regime and is mitigated by PEEP and proning:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A\!-\!a(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(\underbrace{10\bigl(1-g(t)\bigr)+45\,g(t)}_{\text{regime baseline}}-2\,g(t)\bigl(\text{PEEP}(t)-5\bigr)-4\,g(t)\cdot\text{Prone}(t)+\varepsilon_{A\!-\!a}(t),5,80\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>regime baseline</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>PEEP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>Prone</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.102em" rspace="0.102em">−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>80</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A\!-\!a(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(\underbrace{10\bigl(1-g(t)\bigr)+45\,g(t)}_{\text{regime baseline}}-2\,g(t)\bigl(\text{PEEP}(t)-5\bigr)-4\,g(t)\cdot\text{Prone}(t)+\varepsilon_{A\!-\!a}(t),5,80\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Capillary oxygen partial pressure is then:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{a}O_{2}^{\text{cap}}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(P_{A}O_{2}(t)-A\!-\!a(t),30,600\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>cap</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>600</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{a}O_{2}^{\text{cap}}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(P_{A}O_{2}(t)-A\!-\!a(t),30,600\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Shunt and arterial saturation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The shunt fraction rises with regime but is mitigated by PEEP and proning:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{shunt}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(\underbrace{0.05\bigl(1-g(t)\bigr)+0.32\,g(t)}_{\text{regime baseline}}-0.015\,g(t)\bigl(\text{PEEP}(t)-5\bigr)-0.06\,g(t)\,\text{Prone}(t)+\varepsilon_{s}(t),0.02,0.45\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>shunt</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.32</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>regime baseline</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.015</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>PEEP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.06</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Prone</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.02</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.45</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{shunt}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(\underbrace{0.05\bigl(1-g(t)\bigr)+0.32\,g(t)}_{\text{regime baseline}}-0.015\,g(t)\bigl(\text{PEEP}(t)-5\bigr)-0.06\,g(t)\,\text{Prone}(t)+\varepsilon_{s}(t),0.02,0.45\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Capillary oxygen saturation is given by the Hill curve:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{a}O_{2}^{\text{cap}}(t)=\frac{P_{a}O_{2}^{\text{cap}}(t)^{n}}{P_{a}O_{2}^{\text{cap}}(t)^{n}+P50^{n}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>cap</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>cap</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>cap</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>50</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{a}O_{2}^{\text{cap}}(t)=\frac{P_{a}O_{2}^{\text{cap}}(t)^{n}}{P_{a}O_{2}^{\text{cap}}(t)^{n}+P50^{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Finally, the true arterial saturation combines capillary and venous blood according
to the shunt fraction:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{\,S_{a}O_{2}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl((1-\text{shunt}(t))\,S_{a}O_{2}^{\text{cap}}(t)+\text{shunt}(t)\cdot\text{SvO}_{2},0.5,1.0\bigr)=\text{SpO}_{2,\text{true}}(t).\;}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>shunt</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>cap</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>shunt</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>SvO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>SpO</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>true</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{\,S_{a}O_{2}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl((1-\text{shunt}(t))\,S_{a}O_{2}^{\text{cap}}(t)+\text{shunt}(t)\cdot\text{SvO}_{2},0.5,1.0\bigr)=\text{SpO}_{2,\text{true}}(t).\;}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Observation model.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pulse oximetry does not measure <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{a}O_{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{a}O_{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> instantaneously. Instead, the measured saturation <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SpO}_{2}^{\text{obs}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mtext>SpO</mtext><mn>2</mn><mtext>obs</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SpO}_{2}^{\text{obs}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is modeled as a low-pass filtered and noisy version of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SpO}_{2,\text{true}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>SpO</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>true</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SpO}_{2,\text{true}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inertial dynamics.</span> We introduce an exponentially weighted moving average with time constant
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{sens}}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>sens</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{sens}}=10</annotation></semantics></math> seconds. In discrete time this is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{S}(t)=\alpha\,\tilde{S}(t-1)+(1-\alpha)\,S_{a}O_{2}(t),\qquad\alpha=\exp\!\left(-\tfrac{\Delta t}{\tau_{\text{sens}}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>sens</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{S}(t)=\alpha\,\tilde{S}(t-1)+(1-\alpha)\,S_{a}O_{2}(t),\qquad\alpha=\exp\!\left(-\tfrac{\Delta t}{\tau_{\text{sens}}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=60(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=60(s)</annotation></semantics></math> per time step. This smooths sudden changes
in <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{a}O_{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{a}O_{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Measurement noise.</span> Additive Gaussian noise <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon(t)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon(t)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.01</annotation></semantics></math> models sensor variability and motion artefacts.
The final observed saturation is then</p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{\;\text{SpO}_{2}^{\text{obs}}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(\tilde{S}(t)+\varepsilon(t),0.5,1.0\bigr).\;}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>SpO</mtext><mn>2</mn><mtext>obs</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{\;\text{SpO}_{2}^{\text{obs}}(t)=\operatorname{Clip}\bigl(\tilde{S}(t)+\varepsilon(t),0.5,1.0\bigr).\;}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Phase transition (onset of ARDS-like physiology).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The transition is realized as a coordinated change in hidden and semi-hidden physiology driven by <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compliance CL<math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t)</annotation></semantics></math> decreases with <math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math> (stiffer lungs).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Alveolar dead space fraction <math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{DS}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{DS}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> increases with <math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, mildly improved by higher PEEP.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A–a gradient increases with <math id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math> (worsened V/Q), mitigated by PEEP and proning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Shunt increases with <math id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math> (recruitment failure), mitigated by PEEP and proning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.ix5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Auto-PEEP fraction grows due to tachypnea and low compliance, reducing <math id="A1.I1.ix5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and raising PaCO<sub id="A1.I1.ix5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Monolithic Gradient Boosting Regressor Model</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The monolithic gradient boosting regressor model is trained to predict the next-step oxygen saturation <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{t+1\mid t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{t+1\mid t}</annotation></semantics></math> from a feature vector <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The predictor is a gradient-boosted decision tree regressor:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{t+1\mid t}^{\text{mono}}=f^{\text{mono}}(\mathbf{x}_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mtext>mono</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mtext>mono</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{t+1\mid t}^{\text{mono}}=f^{\text{mono}}(\mathbf{x}_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\text{mono}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mtext>mono</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\text{mono}}</annotation></semantics></math> is trained using the feature matrix <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and targets <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Feature set <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The feature matrix for each time <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of 13 features (see Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Digital Twin of Oxygenation Dynamics: Synthetic Physiology and Observation ‣ Flexible Swarm Learning May Outpace Foundation Models in Essential Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> for more details):</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Six raw input features:</span> FiO<sub id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>, PEEP, VT (mL), RR, Prone, and CL (mL/cmH<sub id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Three derived physiology features:</span> <math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{PaCO}_{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>PaCO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{PaCO}_{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{V}_{A}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>V</mtext><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{V}_{A}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> computed from the digital twin formulas using observed inputs (see Eq.s <a href="#A1.E2" title="In Alveolar ventilation and PaCO2. ‣ Appendix A Digital Twin of Oxygenation Dynamics: Synthetic Physiology and Observation ‣ Flexible Swarm Learning May Outpace Foundation Models in Essential Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>–<a href="#A1.E5" title="In Alveolar ventilation and PaCO2. ‣ Appendix A Digital Twin of Oxygenation Dynamics: Synthetic Physiology and Observation ‣ Flexible Swarm Learning May Outpace Foundation Models in Essential Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>), and <math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{P}_{A}\text{O}_{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>P</mtext><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>O</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{P}_{A}\text{O}_{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{P}_{A}\text{O}_{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>P</mtext><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>O</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{P}_{A}\text{O}_{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{FiO_{2}}_{,t}\cdot(P_{b}-P_{\mathrm{H_{2}O}})-\frac{\mathrm{PaCO_{2}}_{,t}}{R}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>FiO</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>PaCO</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{FiO_{2}}_{,t}\cdot(P_{b}-P_{\mathrm{H_{2}O}})-\frac{\mathrm{PaCO_{2}}_{,t}}{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Four input delta features:</span> <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\text{FiO}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>FiO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\text{FiO}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\text{PEEP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>PEEP</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\text{PEEP}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\text{RR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>RR</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\text{RR}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\text{Prone}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Prone</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\text{Prone}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">One-step deltas are</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\mathrm{FiO_{2}}_{,t}=\mathrm{FiO_{2}}_{,t}-\mathrm{FiO_{2}}_{,t-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>FiO</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>FiO</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>FiO</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\mathrm{FiO_{2}}_{,t}=\mathrm{FiO_{2}}_{,t}-\mathrm{FiO_{2}}_{,t-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\mathrm{PEEP}_{t}=\mathrm{PEEP}_{t}-\mathrm{PEEP}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>PEEP</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>PEEP</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>PEEP</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\mathrm{PEEP}_{t}=\mathrm{PEEP}_{t}-\mathrm{PEEP}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\mathrm{RR}_{t}=\mathrm{RR}_{t}-\mathrm{RR}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>RR</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>RR</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>RR</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\mathrm{RR}_{t}=\mathrm{RR}_{t}-\mathrm{RR}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\mathrm{Prone}_{t}=\mathrm{Prone}_{t}-\mathrm{Prone}_{t-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Prone</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Prone</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Prone</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\mathrm{Prone}_{t}=\mathrm{Prone}_{t}-\mathrm{Prone}_{t-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training and early stopping.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The model is trained on pre-transition regions, split into a training prefix and a pre-validation tail.
Hyperparameter tuning is performed via a grid search with early sopping of 10 rounds over learning rate, maximum tree depth, minimum samples per leaf, and subsampling fraction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each configuration, staged prediction on the pre-validation tail determines the optimal number of trees by minimizing the one-step-ahead mean squared error (MSE).
The final model is then refit on the full pre-training window using the selected number of trees.
The chosen hyperparameters are:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{\#n\_estimators}=1200,\quad\text{learning\_rate}=0.01,\quad\text{max\_depth}=3,\quad\text{subsample}=0.7,\quad\text{min\_samples\_leaf}=8." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>#n_estimators</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1200</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>learning_rate</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>max_depth</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>subsample</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>min_samples_leaf</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{\#n\_estimators}=1200,\quad\text{learning\_rate}=0.01,\quad\text{max\_depth}=3,\quad\text{subsample}=0.7,\quad\text{min\_samples\_leaf}=8.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Self-Adaptive Hierarchical Agent Network (SAHA-Net)</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present a hierarchical multi-agent model for one-step-ahead SpO<sub id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub> forecasting.
The model observes SpO<sub id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sub">2</sub> at discrete times <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math> and seeks the
one-step-ahead forecast <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{t+1\mid t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{t+1\mid t}</annotation></semantics></math> from information up to time <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Input vector.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each time step exposes the following input vector:</p>
<table id="A3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}=\big\{\mathrm{FiO}_{2},\mathrm{PEEP},\mathrm{RR},\mathrm{VT},\mathrm{CL},\ \mathrm{Prone},\mathrm{PaCO}_{2},\mathrm{P_{A}O}_{2},\mathrm{V_{A}},\ \Delta\mathrm{FiO}_{2},\ \Delta\mathrm{PEEP},\Delta\mathrm{RR},\Delta\mathrm{Prone}\big\}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>FiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>PEEP</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>RR</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>VT</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>CL</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>Prone</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>PaCO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>FiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>PEEP</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>RR</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Prone</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}=\big\{\mathrm{FiO}_{2},\mathrm{PEEP},\mathrm{RR},\mathrm{VT},\mathrm{CL},\ \mathrm{Prone},\mathrm{PaCO}_{2},\mathrm{P_{A}O}_{2},\mathrm{V_{A}},\ \Delta\mathrm{FiO}_{2},\ \Delta\mathrm{PEEP},\Delta\mathrm{RR},\Delta\mathrm{Prone}\big\}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model hierarchy.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The model is organized as a two-level hierarchy: in the first level, three physiological agents <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> (ventilation/dead space), <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> (A–a gradient), and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> (shunt) receive inputs, and in the second level, a single supervisor agent <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> manages their connections and inputs to produce the final prediction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At the first level of hierarchy, each of the three agents is a gradient boosting regressor that uses masked <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to forecast one-step-ahead SpO<sub id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (ventilation/dead space agent):</span>
this agent tends to favor <math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PEEP},\mathrm{RR},\mathrm{VT},\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>PEEP</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>RR</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>VT</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>CL</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PEEP},\mathrm{RR},\mathrm{VT},\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math>, and their changes, plus <math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{V_{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{V_{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (A–a gradient agent):</span>
this agent tends to favor <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FiO}_{2},\mathrm{PEEP},\mathrm{Prone},\mathrm{P_{A}O}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>FiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>PEEP</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Prone</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FiO}_{2},\mathrm{PEEP},\mathrm{Prone},\mathrm{P_{A}O}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> terms, plus <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PaCO}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>PaCO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PaCO}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{P_{A}O}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{P_{A}O}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (shunt agent):</span>
like the gradient agent, this agent tends to favor <math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FiO}_{2},\mathrm{PEEP},\mathrm{Prone},\mathrm{P_{A}O}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>FiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>PEEP</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Prone</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FiO}_{2},\mathrm{PEEP},\mathrm{Prone},\mathrm{P_{A}O}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> terms, plus <math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PaCO}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>PaCO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PaCO}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{P_{A}O}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{P_{A}O}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These “tendencies” are not hard-coded. Instead, a flexible mask dynamically adapts them, activating or deactivating specific input<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>agent links.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The agents then share their forecasts with one another. A second-level supervisor controls this communication:</p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (supervisor agent):</span>
the supervisor determines which inputs each agent receives, how they communicate, and how their outputs are fused towards the final prediction.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Structuring hierarchical multi-agent networks.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> denote the dimension of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A3.E1" title="In Input vector. ‣ Appendix C Self-Adaptive Hierarchical Agent Network (SAHA-Net) ‣ Flexible Swarm Learning May Outpace Foundation Models in Essential Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>). For each agent <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{A}_{i}\;|\;i\in\{V,G,S\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{A}_{i}\;|\;i\in\{V,G,S\}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a binary mask that selects which coordinates of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
are visible to that agent, and let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(i)}_{t}:=M_{i}\odot u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(i)}_{t}:=M_{i}\odot u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the masked
input (Hadamard product). Each agent produces a private one–step–ahead forecast
from only its masked inputs:</p>
<table id="A3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}^{(i,1)}_{t+1\mid t}\;=\;f^{\mathcal{A}_{i}}\!\big(z^{(i)}_{t};\,\beta_{i}\big),\qquad i\in\{V,G,S\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}^{(i,1)}_{t+1\mid t}\;=\;f^{\mathcal{A}_{i}}\!\big(z^{(i)}_{t};\,\beta_{i}\big),\qquad i\in\{V,G,S\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}(\cdot;\beta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}(\cdot;\beta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is a gradient boosting regressor whose parameters <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are fit on the current training/validation window.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, agents exchange their private predictions. The supervisor maintains
a binary link matrix <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\{0,1\}^{3\times 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\{0,1\}^{3\times 3}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ii}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ii}=0</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j\to i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j\to i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>
permits sending <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}^{(j,1)}_{t+1\mid t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}^{(j,1)}_{t+1\mid t}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. For receiver <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,
define the neighbor set <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{i}:=\{j\neq i:\ C_{j\to i}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{i}:=\{j\neq i:\ C_{j\to i}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The neighbor
aggregate is the uniform mean of permitted senders’ private predictions:</p>
<table id="A3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{y}^{(-i)}_{t+1\mid t}\;=\;\begin{cases}\displaystyle\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}_{i}|}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}}\hat{y}^{(j,1)}_{t+1\mid t},&amp;|\mathcal{N}_{i}|&gt;0,\\[8.0pt]
\hat{y}^{(i,1)}_{t+1\mid t},&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{y}^{(-i)}_{t+1\mid t}\;=\;\begin{cases}\displaystyle\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}_{i}|}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}}\hat{y}^{(j,1)}_{t+1\mid t},&amp;|\mathcal{N}_{i}|&gt;0,\\[8.0pt]
\hat{y}^{(i,1)}_{t+1\mid t},&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the variable set</p>
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\;=\;\big(M_{V},M_{G},M_{S},\ C\big),\quad M_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{d},\ \ C\in\{0,1\}^{3\times 3},\ C_{ii}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\;=\;\big(M_{V},M_{G},M_{S},\ C\big),\quad M_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{d},\ \ C\in\{0,1\}^{3\times 3},\ C_{ii}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">defines the structure of the hierarchical multi-agent network. This parameter set <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is then optimized via a swarm learning strategy.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Updated agent forecasts and supervisor fusion.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Agent <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> updates its forecast by convexly
combining its own private prediction with the neighbor aggregate:</p>
<table id="A3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}^{(i,2)}_{t+1\mid t}\;=\;(1-\lambda_{i})\,\hat{y}^{(i,1)}_{t+1\mid t}\;+\;\lambda_{i}\,\bar{y}^{(-i)}_{t+1\mid t},\qquad\lambda_{i}\in[0,1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}^{(i,2)}_{t+1\mid t}\;=\;(1-\lambda_{i})\,\hat{y}^{(i,1)}_{t+1\mid t}\;+\;\lambda_{i}\,\bar{y}^{(-i)}_{t+1\mid t},\qquad\lambda_{i}\in[0,1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is estimated on the current training/adaptation window by
least squares with projection onto <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is not allowed to become 1. This constraint prevents the agent from effectively self-terminating in an update.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The supervisor constructs a fusion feature vector from the three updated agent
predictions and feeds it to a gradient boosting regressor:</p>
<table id="A3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathrm{sup}}_{t}:=\begin{bmatrix}\hat{y}^{(V,2)}_{t+1\mid t}\\
\hat{y}^{(G,2)}_{t+1\mid t}\\
\hat{y}^{(S,2)}_{t+1\mid t}\end{bmatrix},\qquad\hat{y}_{t+1\mid t}\;=\;f^{\mathcal{S}}\!\left(x^{\mathrm{sup}}_{t};\,\psi\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>sup</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>sup</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathrm{sup}}_{t}:=\begin{bmatrix}\hat{y}^{(V,2)}_{t+1\mid t}\\
\hat{y}^{(G,2)}_{t+1\mid t}\\
\hat{y}^{(S,2)}_{t+1\mid t}\end{bmatrix},\qquad\hat{y}_{t+1\mid t}\;=\;f^{\mathcal{S}}\!\left(x^{\mathrm{sup}}_{t};\,\psi\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed hyperparameters trained on the current window.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Self-adaptive model updates via swarm learning.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the onset of the phase transition, or the switch time. For the pre-switch period (<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>), we employ the prior knowledge-based structure <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M_{i}^{\mathrm{prior}},C^{\mathrm{prior}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>prior</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>prior</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M_{i}^{\mathrm{prior}},C^{\mathrm{prior}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which captures the main feature tendencies of the agents with minimal links between them, and fit all continuous parameters on the pre-switch window. For the post-switch period (<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>), we define a short adaptation window between the switch time and the train/test split point, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{adapt}}=[t^{*},t_{\mathrm{train/test\;split}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>adapt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>train</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>test</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>split</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{adapt}}=[t^{*},t_{\mathrm{train/test\;split}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, during which we adapt the hierarchical structure of the multi-agent system (i.e., the inputs each agent receives and the allowed links) while simultaneously refitting the agent regressors <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\mathcal{A}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\mathcal{A}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the convex weights <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the supervisor <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We then restrict particle swarm optimization to structural variables only:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\;=\;\big(M_{V},M_{G},M_{S},\ C\big),\qquad M_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{d},\ \ C\in\{0,1\}^{3\times 3},\ C_{ii}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\;=\;\big(M_{V},M_{G},M_{S},\ C\big),\qquad M_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{d},\ \ C\in\{0,1\}^{3\times 3},\ C_{ii}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For any candidate <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we:</p>
<ol id="A3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">fit <math id="A3.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}(\cdot;\beta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}(\cdot;\beta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and compute private forecasts (<a href="#A3.E2" title="In Structuring hierarchical multi-agent networks. ‣ Appendix C Self-Adaptive Hierarchical Agent Network (SAHA-Net) ‣ Flexible Swarm Learning May Outpace Foundation Models in Essential Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">form neighbor aggregates (<a href="#A3.E3" title="In Structuring hierarchical multi-agent networks. ‣ Appendix C Self-Adaptive Hierarchical Agent Network (SAHA-Net) ‣ Flexible Swarm Learning May Outpace Foundation Models in Essential Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>) and update agents via
(<a href="#A3.E4" title="In Updated agent forecasts and supervisor fusion. ‣ Appendix C Self-Adaptive Hierarchical Agent Network (SAHA-Net) ‣ Flexible Swarm Learning May Outpace Foundation Models in Essential Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>) (fit <math id="A3.I3.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> by least squares);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">train the supervisor <math id="A3.I3.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> to produce (<a href="#A3.E5" title="In Updated agent forecasts and supervisor fusion. ‣ Appendix C Self-Adaptive Hierarchical Agent Network (SAHA-Net) ‣ Flexible Swarm Learning May Outpace Foundation Models in Essential Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The fitness on <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{adapt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>adapt</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{adapt}}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)\;=\;\frac{1}{|T_{\mathrm{adapt}}|}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{adapt}}}\big(y_{t+1}-\hat{y}_{t+1\mid t}\big)^{2}\;+\;\lambda_{M}\sum_{i\in\{V,G,S\}}\|M_{i}\|_{0}\;+\;\lambda_{C}\,\|C\|_{0}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>adapt</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>adapt</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)\;=\;\frac{1}{|T_{\mathrm{adapt}}|}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{adapt}}}\big(y_{t+1}-\hat{y}_{t+1\mid t}\big)^{2}\;+\;\lambda_{M}\sum_{i\in\{V,G,S\}}\|M_{i}\|_{0}\;+\;\lambda_{C}\,\|C\|_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.4" class="ltx_p">i.e., mean squared error plus small penalties on the number of selected inputs
per agent and the number of active links. We run a modest swarm (30
particles for 30 iterations); particle positions are thresholded to
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> at evaluation time, continuous parameters are refit, and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>
is evaluated with best updates.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
